Files Modified:
- def.h  (Added declarations for the 5 kernel semaphore functions)
- user.h (Added function declarations so user programs can call semaphore operations)
- usys.S (Added "stubs" for semaphore operations) 
- sysproc.c (Added 4 handlers that connect system calls to the semaphore functions in sem.c)
- syscall.h (Added system call number 24-27 for the 4 semaphore system calls)
- syscall.c (Added the system call handlers)
- Makefile (Added sem.o to the kernel objects and _semtest to the user programs)
- main.c (Added seminit() during kernel initialization)

New Files Created:
- sem.c: implements the counting semaphore mechanism inside xv6, uses an array to hold to semaphores. contains 5 functions: seminit(), semalloc(), semwait(), semsignal(), semfree()
- semtest.c: test program to test the semaphore implementation. uses fork() to create 5 child processes. semalloc(2) limits access to critical section to 2 child processes at a time. semalloc(1) to control access to print statements.
